From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: BiSheng <raft-mobile-bisheng@mail.build>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 06:24:13 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(compose): arbitrate native text focus through a
 generation reducer

Native focus/blur callbacks and Compose FocusOwner could fight (focus
self-loops, stale blur clearing a newer editor, retained editors keeping
first responder). KuiklySoftwareKeyboardController now drives an
InputFocusTargetReducer: every native focus/blur command carries a request
id (generation), native focus is only an intent until FocusOwner commits
it, pending focus can be cancelled, detached editors are blurred, retained
focus converges and the keyboard is reshown for an already focused editor.
iOS/Android/OHOS renderers echo focusRequestId, support cancelPendingFocus
and report whether the native focus request was accepted. iOS programmatic
autofocus on textInputState is routed as a focusIntentOnly event instead of
becomeFirstResponder. Native callbacks are bound with updatedNodeEvent so a
retained/prewarmed node never keeps a stale enabled/readOnly policy.
Replaces upstream #1593's `if (!hasFocus)` guard; its empty set(hasFocus)
is kept.

